WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.146 --> 00:00:03.350
(bright music)

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.590
- [Narrator] Some of the
oldest windmills in the world

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.360
can be found on the gusty border

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.466
of northern Iran and Afghanistan.

00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:12.966
(bright electronic music)

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.210
Nashtifan is a city located

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.430
in the Khorasan Province of Iran.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.320
The city name was previously Nishtufan,

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.430
translating to "storm sting,"

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.603
which is appropriate for this windy city.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.280
A 65-foot wall blocks the
intense gale-force winds,

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.930
and on top of that wall
are around two dozen

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.573
vertical axis windmills.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.130
They are made from clay, straw, and wood,

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:47.280
and it's estimated that
they were constructed

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.103
over 1,000 years ago.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.050
The windmills still function today

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.493
and can be used to mill grain into flour.

00:00:58.712 --> 00:01:01.300
In 2002, Nastifan was recognized

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.020
as a National Heritage Site

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.900
by Iran's Cultural Heritage Department,

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.740
in the hopes that it will be around

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.453
for thousands of years to come.

